<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Dutch Treaty of 1814</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Convention of London (1814)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convention of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, also called the Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Treaty of 1814, was signed on 13 August 1814 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>. Britain returned most of the Dutch colonies it had taken in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, but kept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-colony">Cape Colony</a> and the South American colonies of Demerara, Essequibo and Berbice, later united as British Guiana.</p></div>
